Setting. Grothendieck is studying 'lacet' automorphisms. These are automorphisms of the profinite fundamental group π̂_{0,3} of P^1 minus {0,1,∞}, compatible with the extension Ŝ_{0,3}. This extension is the profinite completion of S_{0,3} ≅ PGL(2,Z) (next page). Its index-2 part Ŝ^+_{0,3} is identified with SL(2,Z)^ (previous page). In modern terms this is the problem of describing the Grothendieck–Teichmüller group: elements (λ,f) satisfying the 2-cycle, 3-cycle and λ-relations.

First paragraph. To carry out the mod-6 congruence tests of the previous page (p mod 3, γ ≢ 1 mod 3), he says one must make σ_∞ and f explicit as elements of SL(2,Ẑ). He promises to do this 'tantôt'; the next page, §42 'Récapitulation sur le groupe S_{0,3}', starts that formulary.

Main computation. He returns to his equation (24 bis) and substitutes h_0 = ξ^{-1} ℓ_0^γ. This gives (61): g_0 = φ̂(ξ) ε_0^{γ-β}. A lacet automorphism is thus encoded by data (ξ, g_0, γ, β), with ξ, g_0 ∈ Π_{0,3} and γ, β ∈ Ẑ, subject to (62):
- ξ ρ(ξ) ρ^2(ξ) = 1, the 3-cycle relation;
- ξ · σ_∞(g_0)^{-1} g_0 = ℓ_0^γ, a twisted 2-cycle relation with h = σ_∞(g_0)^{-1} g_0;
- g_0 = φ̂(ξ) ε_0^{γ-β};
- 2γ+1 ∈ Ẑ*, the analogue of λ = 2m+1 being a unit.

Eliminating g_0 and setting r = γ−β, s = γ+β gives (63):
- ξ ρ(ξ) ρ^2(ξ) = 1;
- σ_∞(φ̂(ξ))^{-1} φ̂(ξ) = ε_1^r ξ^{-1} ε_0^s;
- p = r+s+1 ∈ Ẑ*.

Two side remarks.
1. The 3-cycle equation is solved 'cohomologically': ξ = λ ρ(λ)^{-1} or ξ = λ ℓ_0^{-1} ρ(λ)^{-1}. This lists the non-abelian 1-cocycles of Z/3 = ⟨ρ⟩ acting on π̂ up to coboundary. Equivalently, it lists the conjugacy classes of order-3 lifts of ρ in π̂ ⋊ Z/3. There are two, matching the two fixed points e^{±iπ/3} of z ↦ 1/(1−z), i.e. the two order-3 cone points of the quotient orbifold.
2. The residual freedom is ξ' = ℓ_0^α ξ ℓ_1^{-α}, which corresponds to λ' = ℓ_0^α λ. This is the usual ambiguity of f up to multiplication by powers of the generators.
